---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CountyMunicipalityMap from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/CountyMunicipalityMap.astro';
import PublicRecords from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/PublicRecords.astro';
import { leeMunicipalities, leeMunicipalitySources, leeCountyFindings } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/lee';
import { leeCountyRecords } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/lee-records';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Lee County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="County and municipal surveillance research for Lee County, Illinois, including Flock ALPR records, UAS policy, jurisdiction boundaries, and FOIA sources."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <nav class="jurisdiction_breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/illinois/">Illinois</a><span>→</span><strong>Lee County</strong>
  </nav>

  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · LEE COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Lee County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Primary county records document Sheriff use of Flock license-plate readers and an Unmanned Aerial System program policy. Municipality pages remain separate so county equipment is not counted as municipal equipment unless a source actually attributes it to that municipality.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPALITIES · OFFICIAL BOUNDARIES</p>
    <h2>Drill down from Lee County to the municipality.</h2>
    <p>The baseline uses the Illinois State Archives and Lee County planning records. Rochelle crosses Ogle and Lee counties, while the Village of Lee itself straddles DeKalb and Lee counties. Those relationships are represented without duplicating municipal research.</p>

    <div class="map_legend" aria-label="Municipality map legend">
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_covered"></i><strong>Research available</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_open"></i><strong>Unresearched</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_cross_county"></i><strong>Crosses county line</strong></span>
    </div>

    <CountyMunicipalityMap county="Lee" municipalities={leeMunicipalities} />

    <div class="jurisdiction_cards municipality_directory">
      {leeMunicipalities.map(municipality => {
        const isRochelle = municipality.slug === 'rochelle';
        const href = isRochelle
          ? '/illinois/counties/ogle/cities/rochelle/'
          : `/illinois/counties/lee/cities/${municipality.slug}/`;
        return (
          <a href={href}>
            <strong>{municipality.name}</strong>
            <span>{municipality.form.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + municipality.form.slice(1)} · {municipality.status === 'partial' || municipality.status === 'documented' ? 'Municipal dossier available' : 'Research needed'}{municipality.crossCounty ? ` · crosses ${municipality.counties.join(' / ')} counties` : ''}</span>
          </a>
        );
      })}
    </div>

    <p class="map_note">
      <a href={leeMunicipalitySources.stateArchives}>Illinois State Archives local-government index</a> ·
      <a href={leeMunicipalitySources.countyPlan}>Lee County comprehensive plan</a> ·
      <a href={leeMunicipalitySources.leeCrossCounty}>Village of Lee cross-county confirmation</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">LEE COUNTY SHERIFF</p>
    <h2>Documented surveillance systems.</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      {leeCountyFindings.map(finding => (
        <article>
          <span class="status_label">{finding.status.toUpperCase()}</span>
          <p class="eyebrow finding_technology">{finding.technology}</p>
          <h3>{finding.title}</h3>
          <p>{finding.summary}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence_box evidence_unknown">
    <span class="status_label">COUNT NOT CURRENTLY RESOLVED</span>
    <h2>Do not turn the FY2025 six-camera budget line into a 2026 inventory.</h2>
    <p>The county record establishes that six Flock LPR cameras were budgeted for the Sheriff and later records confirm operational Flock use. NoRec has not yet obtained a current camera inventory, current installation list, retention configuration, sharing configuration, or complete audit history, so those remain unresolved.</p>
  </section>

  <PublicRecords records={leeCountyRecords} />

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">NEXT RECORDS</p>
    <h2>High-value follow-up.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>Current Lee County Sheriff Flock inventory, serials/asset IDs, installation coordinates, and status.</li>
      <li>Flock contract, invoices, renewal terms, retention settings, sharing configuration, hotlists, and search/audit logs.</li>
      <li>Current Sheriff UAS inventory, make/model/serial, payloads, flight logs, public notices, and annual reports.</li>
      <li>Body-worn/in-car camera vendor, inventory, retention, and cloud evidence contracts.</li>
      <li>Social-media analytics, facial-recognition, fixed-camera, and other investigative software contracts or policies.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
